{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/644825-have-you-ever-tweaked-bloodlines","id":644825,"title":"Have you ever tweaked Bloodlines?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-29T19:08:36-07:00","id":644825,"title":"Have you ever tweaked Bloodlines?","content":"I have a lot of love for Bloodlines; I think they really helped flesh out the diverse, mutable and mysterious nature of vampires. That said, I haven't always agreed with the crunch of them, and so I've sometimes taken matters into my own hands. For example, I really don't see why the Noktuku are a Nosferatu Bloodline beyond the obvious Mythology Gag to the OWoD; the diablerist who mutates into a &quot;true&quot; predator of vampires seems so rich and broad an archetype. Consequently, in my games, I've made them one of the rare Bloodlines that any vampire can join, but which is easiest to join if you've committed diablerie - Nosferatu and Gangrel are more likely to be Noktuku because they are most likely to be on the fringes of Kindred society to begin with.<br /> <br /> So, I was curious if anyone else has ever tweaked the crunch of one more Bloodlines in their games, and how you did so if that's the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T20:22:31-07:00","id":644894,"title":"","content":"I've done it so often I can't even remember them all. It's a part of being a Storyteller to be honest, making the concept fit the setting.<br /> <br /> I do remember a big change I made was allowing Diablerie to be used to gain the unique Disciplines of a Bloodline even if you weren't a member of it. But to increase the dots I set the ridiculously high XP cost of x10","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T03:54:32-07:00","id":645237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/644825-have-you-ever-tweaked-bloodlines#post644825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a lot of love for Bloodlines; I think they really helped flesh out the diverse, mutable and mysterious nature of vampires. That said, I haven't always agreed with the crunch of them, and so I've sometimes taken matters into my own hands. For example, I really don't see why the Noktuku are a Nosferatu Bloodline beyond the obvious Mythology Gag to the OWoD; the diablerist who mutates into a &quot;true&quot; predator of vampires seems so rich and broad an archetype. Consequently, in my games, I've made them one of the rare Bloodlines that any vampire can join, but which is easiest to join if you've committed diablerie - Nosferatu and Gangrel are more likely to be Noktuku because they are most likely to be on the fringes of Kindred society to begin with.<br /> <br /> So, I was curious if anyone else has ever tweaked the crunch of one more Bloodlines in their games, and how you did so if that's the case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think the idea of becoming a predator that other predators fear makes the Noktuku feel more like a Gangrel bloodline. One might argue they're the only true predators among the kindred. Most vampires feed exclusively on blood, they're more like parasites. <b>The Noktuku eat flesh!</b><br /> <br /> I wasn't too happy to find the Brujah who at least had a modicum of history they could be proud of were reduced to a bunch of hell raising bikers and street punks. Now they couldn't even claim they were once philosophers, they're just miscreant thugs and street level criminals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T05:47:49-07:00","id":645306,"title":"","content":"There's strong hints that the &quot;founder&quot; of the Bruja is not the actual founder, just a vampire that awakened his latent lineage of a bloodine lost to the ages. I favor that interpretation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: even more on topic I used my own Morbus version in my New Orleans game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T15:44:03-07:00","id":645965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/644825-have-you-ever-tweaked-bloodlines?p=644894#post644894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've done it so often I can't even remember them all. It's a part of being a Storyteller to be honest, making the concept fit the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree with this, So many tweaks and alterations here or there that it becomes hard to track. But a story tellers job is to make everything work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7529-silentstaccato","name":"SilentStaccato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7529_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}